-- title:
--   Both degeneracy traces vanish on a q-new local component
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ and $q$ be nonzero natural numbers and let `h1`, `hq'` witness the relation [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) between the levels $M$ and $Mq$ with full unit subgroups and shift $1$, resp. $q$; concretely, $M \mid Mq$, $1 \mid Mq/M$, resp. $q \mid Mq/M$, together with the (here vacuous) condition that reduction carries $\top \le (\mathbb{Z}/Mq)^\times$ into $\top \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Let $S$ be a set of naturals and $\mathcal{O}$ a noetherian local commutative ring with residue field $k$. Write $H^1(L) = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L)^{\mathrm{add}}, \mathcal{O})$ for $L = Mq, M$ at $H = \top$, and let [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) be the family of endomorphisms of $H^1(L)$ indexed by [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13), whose constructors are $T_\ell$ for $\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$, $U_r$ for $r$ prime dividing $L$ (both realised by `heckeTL`, a corestriction construction), and diamond operators $\langle d\rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$. Assume `hcomm`, `hcommM`: these operators commute pairwise at levels $Mq$ and $M$. Fix arbitrary functions $\bar\theta$, $\bar\theta_M$ from the respective generator types to $k$; the resulting [`CohCarrier.hdata`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L96) has `opSubalgebra` the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{T}$ of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}} H^1$ generated by the range of the operator family. Let `Sp` be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $\mathbb{T}_{Mq}$, i.e. finitely many complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ iff $i \ne j$; fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0}\mathbb{T}_{Mq}e_{i_0}$ to $k$ sending the corner of each generator's operator to its $\bar\theta$-value. Let `SpM` be such a splitting of $\mathbb{T}_M$, and assume that for every index $i'$ of `SpM` there is a polynomial $f$ over $\mathcal{O}$ in variables indexed by the primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid Mq$ whose value at the scalars $\bar\theta(T_\ell)$ is $0$ in $k$, while its value at the corresponding operators $T_\ell \in \mathbb{T}_M$ does not lie in $\mathfrak{m}_{i'}$. Then for every $v \in H^1(Mq)$ lying in [`IharaLemma.cornerSubmodule`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L46) of $e_{i_0}$, that is in the image of multiplication by $e_{i_0}$, both transfer maps [`CohCarrier.jDeg`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L482) with shift $1$ and with shift $q$ annihilate $v$.
--
--   This is the assertion that the local component of $H^1(\Gamma_0(Mq),\mathcal{O})$ cut out by the idempotent of a residual Hecke eigensystem $\bar\theta$ which is congruent at the good primes to no maximal ideal of the level-$M$ Hecke algebra is new at $q$: both degeneracy traces down to level $M$ vanish on it. It is used in the level-raising step at a prime exactly dividing the level, where the vanishing of the trace for shift $1$ reduces the composite of the raising and lowering maps to a unit multiple of $U_q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CohCarrier_jDeg_apply_eq_zero_of_mem_cornerSubmodule_of_forall_notMem.lean

